# Code owners for constitutional and enforcement paths.
#
# The owner is a machine account holding its own credential — NOT the account
# the operator writes with. GitHub does not count a pull request author's own
# approval, so an operator that is also the code owner would deadlock every
# change it makes. That is why this file names federation-operator and not the
# repository owner.
#
# What this buys: a change to any path below cannot merge until a second
# identity approves it, at the moment the diff exists. The consultation gate
# proves a transcript exists; this proves someone with a different credential
# pressed a button. Neither proves a review happened — see CLAUDE.md.
#
# An earlier CODEOWNERS was removed in 92af56c on the premise that required
# code-owner review is unavailable on the free tier. That premise was wrong for
# a public repository; verified by API on 2026-07-26 (#61).

# The constitution and its adoption record
/CLAUDE.md                          @federation-operator
/docs/founding-package-v0.2.md      @federation-operator
/docs/founding-decision-record.md   @federation-operator
/docs/amendments.md                 @federation-operator
/docs/*-adr.md                      @federation-operator

# The governance apparatus itself
/governance/                        @federation-operator

# The enforcement machinery — the referee must not be replaceable by the
# players. scripts/ and schemas/ carry the gate, the validators and the
# determinism checks; a PR "refactoring" them can dismantle every control in
# this repository with green CI (round-4 review of #57).
/scripts/                           @federation-operator
/schemas/                           @federation-operator
/.github/                           @federation-operator

# The execution and rights boundary — /core/ carries the sandbox profile,
# the sudo-invoked wrappers and the capability policy.  A PR changing
# them can widen the boundary with green CI, so a second credential
# must approve.
/core/                              @federation-operator
